---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';
import { CONTACT } from '../../data/site';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Funerals we arrange', url: '/funeral-services/' },
  { name: 'Burial', url: '/funeral-services/burial/' },
];
---

<Page
  title="Burial in Dunbar, East Lothian & Berwickshire"
  heading="Burial"
  description="Arranging a burial in East Lothian or Berwickshire: choosing a lair, reopening a family grave, costs and what to expect. John Bald Funeral Directors, Dunbar."
  standfirst="In a local churchyard, a council cemetery, or a family lair that has been waiting a long time."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <p>
    Burial is still what many families in this part of Scotland choose, particularly where
    there is an existing family grave. We arrange burials throughout East Lothian and
    Berwickshire and know the local cemeteries and their keepers well.
  </p>

  <h2>Choosing where</h2>
  <p>
    In East Lothian, burial grounds are managed by East Lothian Council; in Berwickshire,
    by Scottish Borders Council. Some churchyards are managed by the church itself. We
    have set out every burial ground in the region, with who manages it and how to
    enquire about a lair, in our{' '}
    <a href="/directory/cemeteries/">cemetery directory</a>.
  </p>

  <h3>An existing family lair</h3>
  <p>
    If the family already holds a lair, it can usually be reopened. We will need to trace
    the lair certificate — the deed showing who holds the burial rights — and get the
    written permission of whoever holds them. If nobody can find the certificate, do not
    panic. The council keeps its own records and we can almost always trace it. Allow a
    little longer for the funeral if we are working from council records.
  </p>
  <p>
    A grave can be reopened only if there is room and if the depth allows. The council
    will confirm this before anything is arranged.
  </p>

  <h3>A new lair</h3>
  <p>
    Where a family has no existing grave, we will help you choose and purchase a new lair.
    You are buying the exclusive right of burial for a set period, not the land itself.
    That right can be passed on, and it is what allows the grave to be reopened later.
  </p>

  <Callout title="Worth knowing before you decide">
    <p>
      Burial usually costs more than cremation, mostly because of the lair purchase and
      the interment fee, both of which are council charges rather than ours. If cost is a
      concern, say so early — it is a completely ordinary thing to weigh, and there is
      often <a href="/funeral-costs/help-with-funeral-costs/">help available</a>.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h2>What the day looks like</h2>
  <p>
    Most families have a service first — in a church, at our funeral home, or at the
    graveside itself — and then go to the cemetery for the committal. Some have only the
    graveside service. Both are entirely usual.
  </p>
  <p>
    We will carry the coffin, or arrange for family to carry if you would like to. A lot
    of people find that they want to and had not realised it was allowed. It is.
  </p>

  <h2>What it costs</h2>
  <p>
    Our own fee is on our{' '}
    <a href="/funeral-costs/standardised-price-list/">Standardised Price List</a>. On top
    of that sit two council charges we pay on your behalf and pass on without markup:
    the lair purchase, where a new grave is needed, and the interment fee. These vary
    between East Lothian and Scottish Borders and change each April.
  </p>
  <p>
    There is no interment fee in Scotland for anyone under 18.{' '}
    <a href="/funeral-services/childrens-funerals/">More about children's funerals</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Memorials</h2>
  <p>
    A headstone cannot go up straight away — the ground needs several months to settle,
    usually between six and twelve. Cemeteries also have rules about size, material and
    inscription. We will tell you what is allowed where, and there is no hurry at all.{' '}
    <a href="/memorials/">More about memorials</a>.
  </p>

  <Callout tone="accent">
    <p>
      To talk about a burial, telephone{' '}
      <a href={CONTACT.phoneHref} class="font-semibold">{CONTACT.phone}</a>.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h2>Related</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/funeral-services/natural-burial/">Natural and woodland burial</a></li>
    <li><a href="/directory/cemeteries/">Cemeteries across the east of Scotland</a></li>
    <li><a href="/guides/burial-or-cremation/">Choosing between burial and cremation</a></li>
  </ul>
</Page>
